### =====================================================================
###  Demo requests - all go through the API GATEWAY (port 5000).
###  VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request".
###  Visual Studio / Rider support .http files natively.
### =====================================================================

@gateway = http://localhost:5000

@laptop     = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@phone      = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@headphones = 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333
@watch      = 44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444

### Gateway info
GET {{gateway}}/

### List products (note the stock quantities, check again after orders)
GET {{gateway}}/api/products/


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### SCENARIO 1 - HAPPY PATH  (total 259.98 <= 1000)
### Saga: ReserveStock -> StockReserved -> ProcessPayment -> PaymentSucceeded -> Confirmed
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name happyOrder
POST {{gateway}}/api/orders/
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: demo-happy-path-001

{
  "customerEmail": "alice@example.com",
  "items": [ { "productId": "{{headphones}}", "quantity": 2 } ]
}

### Order status (poll after ~1 second: Pending -> Confirmed)
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders/{{happyOrder.response.body.orderId}}

### Saga timeline for that order
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders/{{happyOrder.response.body.orderId}}/saga


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### SCENARIO 2 - PAYMENT FAILS -> COMPENSATION  (laptop = 1499 > 1000 limit)
### Saga: ReserveStock -> StockReserved -> ProcessPayment -> PaymentFailed
###       -> ReleaseStock (compensation) -> StockReleased -> Cancelled
### Check product stock before/after: it must be unchanged in the end.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name failedPayment
POST {{gateway}}/api/orders/
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: demo-compensation-001

{
  "customerEmail": "bob@example.com",
  "items": [ { "productId": "{{laptop}}", "quantity": 1 } ]
}

###
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders/{{failedPayment.response.body.orderId}}/saga


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### SCENARIO 3 - OUT OF STOCK  (watch has only 2 in stock)
### Saga: ReserveStock -> StockReservationFailed -> Cancelled (nothing to compensate)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name outOfStock
POST {{gateway}}/api/orders/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "carol@example.com",
  "items": [ { "productId": "{{watch}}", "quantity": 5 } ]
}

###
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders/{{outOfStock.response.body.orderId}}/saga


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### SCENARIO 4 - CIRCUIT BREAKER
###  1) enable chaos  2) send the order 2-3 times (each = 3 attempts with retries)
###  3) circuit OPENS -> next order fails instantly with 503
###  4) disable chaos, wait 20s -> HALF-OPEN -> next order succeeds -> CLOSED
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{gateway}}/api/products/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "enabled": true, "delayMs": 0 }

### Place an order while ProductService is "broken" (repeat this a few times)
POST {{gateway}}/api/orders/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "dave@example.com",
  "items": [ { "productId": "{{phone}}", "quantity": 1 } ]
}

### Circuit state: Closed / Open / HalfOpen
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders/circuit-breaker

### Heal the service
POST {{gateway}}/api/products/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "enabled": false, "delayMs": 0 }


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Other endpoints
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders/

###
GET {{gateway}}/api/payments/

### Create a product
POST {{gateway}}/api/products/
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "USB-C Cable", "description": "1m", "price": 9.99, "stockQuantity": 500 }

### Health (gateway). Service health endpoints are internal: /health/live and /health/ready
GET {{gateway}}/health/ready
